:{"derivedAnswer":"5/18","reason":"The probability is (5/10)(5/9) = 25/90 = 5/18; after a red draw, all five blue balls remain among nine balls.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_h245_q2","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h244","cnm_p178"],"id":"cnm_h245_q2_m1","label":"Condition on the first draw","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_h245_q2_m1":["cnm_310","cnm_h245"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_310","cnm_h245","cnm_h244","cnm_p178"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"cnm_h245_q2_m2","label":"Count ordered pairs of balls","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_h245_q2_m2":["cnm_310","cnm_h231","cnm_309"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_310","cnm_h231","cnm_309"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A, 4/9","reason":"There are five balls of each parity. Whatever Jack draws, exactly four of the nine remaining balls have matching parity, giving probability 4/9.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1987_AMC_8_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p156","cnm_p165"],"id":"matching-parity","label":"Count matching odd or even numbers","methodDirectNodeIds":{"matching-parity":["cnm_285","cnm_310"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_285","cnm_310","cnm_p156","cnm_p165"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 1/5","reason":"The minimum sum of three distinct chips is 1+2+3=6. The qualifying first-two-draw outcomes are (1,2), (2,1), (1,3), and (3,1). There are 5×4=20 equally likely ordered pairs, so the probability is 4/20=1/5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2018_AMC_10B_Q06","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_287"],"id":"count-two-draw-prefixes","label":"Enumerate the first two draws","methodDirectNodeIds":{"count-two-draw-prefixes":["cnm_286","cnm_310","cnm_285"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_287","cnm_286","cnm_310","cnm_285"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 1/2","reason":"There are C(8,2)=28 bill pairs. Exactly C(8,2)-C(6,2)=13 contain a twenty, and one additional pair consists of the two tens. The probability is 14/28=1/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2005_AMC_12B_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_309","cnm_h236","cnm_h231","cnm_h230"],"id":"disjoint_bill_pairs","label":"Count qualifying pairs","methodDirectNodeIds":{"disjoint_bill_pairs":["cnm_h137","cnm_310","cnm_h239"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h137","cnm_310","cnm_h239","cnm_309","cnm_h236","cnm_h231","cnm_h230"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D (3/5)","reason":"Imagine continuing until all five chips are drawn. The stopping chip is white exactly when both whites occur before the last red, equivalently when the final chip in the complete order is red. That probability is 3/5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2001_AMC_12_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_310","cnm_309"],"id":"complete-random-order","label":"Imagine the complete draw order","methodDirectNodeIds":{"complete-random-order":["cnm_h137"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h137","cnm_310","cnm_309"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 1/5","reason":"There are C(6,2) = 15 equally likely final pairs. Each of the three colors supplies exactly one monochromatic pair, so the probability is 3/15 = 1/5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2015_AMC_12A_Q09","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_309","cnm_310"],"id":"random-pair-companion","label":"Count the possible companions","methodDirectNodeIds":{"random-pair-companion":["cnm_285"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_285","cnm_309","cnm_310"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 9/28","reason":"Consider the bands assigned to the three tallest athletes. After the first band, 6 of the remaining 8 have another color. After two different colors, 3 of the remaining 7 have the third color. Therefore the probability is (6/8)(3/7)=9/28.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2025_AMC_10B_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"sequential-band-draws","label":"Sequential draws without replacement","methodDirectNodeIds":{"sequential-band-draws":["cnm_h137","cnm_h245","cnm_310"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h245","cnm_h137","cnm_310"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"unordered-band-sample","label":"Count three-band samples","methodDirectNodeIds":{"unordered-band-sample":["cnm_h137","cnm_h239","cnm_310"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h239","cnm_h137","cnm_310"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 9/28","reason":"After the tallest athlete receives a color, the next tallest receives a different color with probability 6/8. The third then receives the remaining color with probability 3/7. Their product is 9/28.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2025_AMC_12B_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"sequential-band-draws","label":"Follow the three tallest","methodDirectNodeIds":{"sequential-band-draws":["cnm_h137","cnm_h245","cnm_310"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h137","cnm_h245","cnm_310"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"unordered-band-sample","label":"Count sets of three bands","methodDirectNodeIds":{"unordered-band-sample":["cnm_h137","cnm_h239","cnm_310"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h137","cnm_h239","cnm_310"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C. 1/7","reason":"The triples summing to 6 are